description:
## Goal

The settings of `mairc`: where its files live, the defaults, validation, loading and saving `config.json`, and
the `mairc config` subcommand's logic.

## Files you own

`internal/config/*.go` (package `config`) and its tests. Nothing else.

## What exists already

`internal/core/core.go` defines `core.Settings` (13 fields with JSON tags) and `core.DefaultSettings()`.
Use them; do not redefine them.

## API to implement (exact names; other beads call these)

```go
package config

// Paths are the files of one mairc installation.
type Paths struct{ Home, Config, DB, Token, Log, PID string }

// ResolvePaths returns the paths under $MAIRC_HOME, else $XDG_DATA_HOME/mairc, else $HOME/.local/share/mairc.
// File names: config.json, mairc.db, token, daemon.log, daemon.pid. getenv is os.Getenv in production.
func ResolvePaths(getenv func(string) string) (Paths, error)

// EnsureHome creates Home with mode 0700 if missing.
func EnsureHome(p Paths) error

// Load reads the settings file. A missing file returns the defaults and no error.
// Keys absent from the file keep their defaults. An unknown key or an invalid value is an error naming the key.
func Load(path string) (core.Settings, error)

// Save writes the settings as indented JSON, atomically (temp file in the same directory, fsync, rename), mode 0600.
func Save(path string, s core.Settings) error

// Validate checks every field against its range.
func Validate(s core.Settings) error

// Keys lists the setting keys in the order of the table below.
func Keys() []string

// Get returns one setting as text ("256", "true", "127.0.0.1:4747").
func Get(s core.Settings, key string) (string, error)

// Set parses value for key, stores it in s and validates the result. Booleans accept true/false/on/off/1/0.
func Set(s *core.Settings, key, value string) error

// ReadToken returns the trimmed content of the token file.
func ReadToken(path string) (string, error)

// Run implements `mairc config`: with no arguments it prints every "key = value" line in Keys() order;
// `get <key>` prints the value; `set <key> <value>` loads, sets, saves and prints "key = value".
// It writes to out and errOut and returns the process exit code (0 ok, 1 error, 2 usage).
// After a successful set it calls reload(), which the caller wires to the daemon; a reload error is printed to
// errOut as "saved; daemon not reloaded: <err>" and still returns 0.
func Run(args []string, p Paths, out, errOut io.Writer, reload func() error) int
```

## The settings (key, range, default)

| Key | Range | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `max_private_len` | 1–999 | 256 |
| `max_public_len` | 1–999 | 256 |
| `max_room_lines` | 1–100 | 10 |
| `private_enabled` | bool | true |
| `public_enabled` | bool | true |
| `private_cooldown_s` | 0–86400 | 60 |
| `public_cooldown_s` | 0–86400 | 60 |
| `keep_messages` | 1–1000000 | 1000 |
| `keep_hours` | 1–8760 | 24 |
| `check_private_every` | 1–1000 | 1 |
| `check_room_every` | 1–1000 | 10 |
| `listen` | `host:port`, host must be a loopback address (`127.0.0.1`, `::1`, `localhost`), port 1–65535 | `127.0.0.1:4747` |
| `hook_timeout_ms` | 50–5000 | 300 |

Error texts (exact): `unknown setting: <key>`, `<key>: must be between <min> and <max>`,
`<key>: must be true or false`, `listen: must be a loopback host:port`.

## Tests

- defaults equal the table; `Keys()` order equals the table;
- every numeric key: min, max, min-1, max+1; `listen` with a non-loopback host is refused;
- `Load`: missing file → defaults; partial file keeps other defaults; unknown key and bad value name the key;
- `Save` then `Load` round-trips; the file is mode 0600; a failed write leaves the old file intact;
- `Set` with each boolean spelling; `Get` for every key;
- `Run`: the three forms, exit codes, the reload call and the `saved; daemon not reloaded` line;
- `ResolvePaths` for the three environment cases.
- Golden file: `testdata/vectors/config.default.json` is what `Save` writes for the defaults (create it; the test
  compares byte for byte).

## Not in this bead

Starting or reloading the daemon (the `cli` bead wires `reload`), the token's creation (the `daemon` bead).

## Working rules (the same for every bead)

- **Project in three lines:** `mairc` is a tiny chat system for coding agents, served as an MCP server. A
  background daemon owns one SQLite file; agents reach it through a stdio shim, Streamable HTTP, and a hook that
  prints nothing when there is nothing to read. One public room, private messages, nothing else.
- **No scope creep.** Build exactly what this bead says. If something seems missing, write it in the bead's notes
  and ask; do not add features, flags, settings or dependencies.
- **Toolchain:** Go 1.27.4. `export PATH=$HOME/sdk/go1.27.4/bin:$HOME/go/bin:$PATH`. Build with `CGO_ENABLED=0`.
- **Contract:** `internal/core/core.go` holds the shared types and interfaces. Use them as they are. Do not edit
  that file unless this bead says so.
- **Rust-port readiness:** standard library first; the only third-party dependency allowed in the whole project is
  `modernc.org/sqlite`, and only in `internal/store`. No reflection tricks, no code generation, no global mutable
  state, no `init()` side effects, no panics for control flow. Errors are values with stable short texts.
- **Tests:** table-driven, `testing` only (no assertion libraries), a fake clock, temporary directories, no
  sleeps, no network beyond loopback. Every user-visible string named in this bead is asserted verbatim.
- **Before you push:** `gofumpt -l . && go vet ./... && golangci-lint run && go test -race -count=1 ./...`, all
  clean. If `.golangci.yml` is not in the repository yet, run `golangci-lint run` with its defaults.
- **Stay in your files.** Touch only the paths listed under "Files you own". Remove the `.gitkeep` in a directory
  when you add its first real file.
- **Beads:** claim with `br update <id> --claim --actor "<model> (<your name>)"`, close with
  `br close <id> --reason "<commit> + the tests that prove it"`. Commit `.beads/issues.jsonl` with your work, name
  the bead id in the commit message, `git pull --rebase` then push to `main`.
